      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To handle partial and final streaming recognition events, I will use the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API. This API provides streaming speech recognition, which is suitable for handling real-time audio data. I will import the necessary client library and set up a streaming recognizer to process audio chunks and yield both partial and final recognition results. The provider-specific client class and API hostname will be included to make the integration identifiable. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
